{"traceId":"d64df6cacccd7f9a48b1a2a477c2e7e7","displayName":"travelItineraryFlow","startTime":1790578772674,"endTime":1790578788365.8572,"spans":{"64f7a772d7cde725":{"spanId":"64f7a772d7cde725","traceId":"d64df6cacccd7f9a48b1a2a477c2e7e7","startTime":1790578772674,"endTime":1790578788365.8572,"attributes":{"genkit:type":"action","genkit:metadata:subtype":"flow","genkit:key":"/flow/travelItineraryFlow","genkit:name":"travelItineraryFlow","genkit:isRoot":true,"genkit:path":"/{travelItineraryFlow,t:flow}","genkit:input":"\"Make a 20-day trip itinerary from India to Japan\"","genkit:output":"\"20-DAY JAPAN TRIP ITINERARY FOR STUDENTS\\n\\nTRIP ROUTE\\nTokyo - Hakone & Mt. Fuji - Kyoto - Nara - Osaka - Hiroshima - Tokyo\\n\\n---\\n\\nDAY-WISE PLAN\\n\\nDay 1: Arrival in Tokyo\\n* Fly from India to Tokyo (Narita or Haneda Airport).\\n* Pick up your pocket Wi-Fi and IC travel card (Suica or Pasmo).\\n* Check in to your hostel and rest.\\n\\nDay 2: Modern Tokyo\\n* Walk across the famous Shibuya Crossing.\\n* Take a photo with the Hachiko Statue.\\n* Explore trendy youth fashion on Takeshita Street in Harajuku.\\n* Visit the quiet Meiji Shrine.\\n\\nDay 3: Traditional Tokyo and Anime Hub\\n* Visit Senso-ji Temple in Asakusa.\\n* Shop for small souvenirs along Nakamise Street.\\n* Spend the afternoon in Akihabara, the center of anime and video games.\\n\\nDay 4: City Views and Gardens\\n* Walk through Shinjuku Gyoen National Garden.\\n* Get a free view of Tokyo from the Tokyo Metropolitan Government Building.\\n* Visit Tokyo Skytree or Tokyo Tower in the evening.\\n\\nDay 5: High-Tech Tokyo\\n* Head to the artificial island of Odaiba.\\n* See the giant moving Unicorn Gundam statue.\\n* Visit teamLab Planets for an interactive digital art show.\\n\\nDay 6: Day Trip to Kamakura\\n* Take a 1-hour train ride to the coastal town of Kamakura.\\n* See the Great Buddha (Kotoku-in).\\n* Walk along Yuigahama Beach before heading back to Tokyo.\\n\\nDay 7: Tokyo to Hakone\\n* Take the train to Hakone using the Hakone Freepass.\\n* Ride the cable car and ropeway over volcanic valleys.\\n* Cruise on Lake Ashi in a pirate ship and look for Mt. Fuji.\\n* Stay at a budget guesthouse with a hot spring bath (Onsen).\\n\\nDay 8: Mt. Fuji Views\\n* Take a local bus to Lake Kawaguchiko.\\n* Visit the Chureito Pagoda for the postcard view of Mt. Fuji.\\n* Walk along the lake and rent a cheap bicycle.\\n\\nDay 9: Journey to Kyoto\\n* Take a highway bus or train from Kawaguchiko to Kyoto.\\n* Check into your Kyoto hostel.\\n* Take a peaceful evening walk through the historic Gion district.\\n\\nDay 10: Iconic Kyoto\\n* Wake up early to walk through the thousands of red gates at Fushimi Inari Shrine.\\n* Visit Kiyomizu-dera Temple and enjoy the hillside view.\\n* Walk down the preserved streets of Ninenzaka and Sannenzaka.\\n\\nDay 11: Nature and Monkeys\\n* Visit the Arashiyama Bamboo Grove in the early morning.\\n* Hike up to the Iwatayama Monkey Park to feed wild monkeys.\\n* Walk across the scenic Togetsukyo Bridge.\\n\\nDay 12: Golden Pavilion and Markets\\n* Visit Kinkaku-ji, the famous Golden Pavilion.\\n* Try lots of street food at Nishiki Market.\\n* Relax by the Kamogawa River in the evening.\\n\\nDay 13: Day Trip to Uji\\n* Take a quick 30-minute train to Uji, the green tea capital.\\n* Visit the Byodoin Temple (shown on the 10-yen coin).\\n* Taste authentic matcha ice cream and green tea ramen.\\n\\nDay 14: Friendly Deer and Move to Osaka\\n* Take a morning train to Nara.\\n* Bow to the free-roaming deer in Nara Park.\\n* Visit Todai-ji Temple to see the giant bronze Buddha.\\n* Take an evening train to Osaka and check in.\\n\\nDay 15: Heart of Osaka\\n* Visit the historic Osaka Castle and its park.\\n* Explore the retro neighborhood of Shinsekai.\\n* Spend the night under the neon signs and giant crab of Dotonbori.\\n\\nDay 16: Theme Park or City Culture\\n* Option A: Spend a full day at Universal Studios Japan (Super Nintendo World).\\n* Option B: Visit the Osaka Aquarium (Kaiyukan) and thrift-shop in Amerikamura.\\n\\nDay 17: Day Trip to Kobe\\n* Take a 30-minute train to the port city of Kobe.\\n* Walk around Harborland and Chinatown (Nankinmachi).\\n* Try a budget lunch set of world-famous Kobe beef.\\n\\nDay 18: Osaka to Hiroshima\\n* Take the Shinkansen (bullet train) to Hiroshima.\\n* Visit the Hiroshima Peace Memorial Park and Atomic Bomb Dome.\\n* Walk through the Peace Memorial Museum to learn about history.\\n\\nDay 19: Miyajima Island and Back to Tokyo\\n* Take a short ferry ride to Miyajima Island.\\n* See the \\\"floating\\\" Torii gate of Itsukushima Shrine.\\n* Take the evening bullet train or a cheap overnight bus back to Tokyo.\\n\\nDay 20: Tokyo and Fly Home\\n* Buy snacks and gifts at Don Quijote or 100-yen stores.\\n* Head to the airport.\\n* Fly back to India.\\n\\n---\\n\\nMUST-TRY LOCAL FOOD\\n\\n* Onigiri: Rice balls wrapped in seaweed, sold at convenience stores for very cheap.\\n* Ramen: Warm noodle soup with rich broth (pork, chicken, or vegetarian).\\n* Takoyaki: Fried batter balls filled with octopus, topped with sauce and mayo.\\n* Okonomiyaki: Savory cabbage pancake grilled on a hot plate.\\n* Gyudon: Quick and tasty bowl of rice topped with thinly sliced beef (found at chains like Sukiya and Yoshinoya).\\n* Dango & Mochi: Sweet, chewy rice cakes on skewers.\\n* Matcha Soft Serve: Rich green tea ice cream.\\n\\n---\\n\\nBUDGET TIPS FOR STUDENTS\\n\\n* Stay in Hostels: Book dorm beds or capsule hotels. They are super clean, safe, and cost a fraction of hotel rooms.\\n* Eat at Convenience Stores: Konbini (7-Eleven, FamilyMart, Lawson) have fresh meals, sandwiches, and bento boxes for under 500 yen (approx. 280 INR).\\n* Save on Long-Distance Travel: Instead of the expensive national JR Pass, use night buses (like Willer Express) between Tokyo and Kyoto to save on both travel and a night of accommodation.\\n* Free Water: Tap water across Japan is completely safe to drink. Carry a